# Call-site ledger of argcomplete at 0571dc489d9543b40f1bcbc6cbac4377906b76fd.
# Hand-written from the source; judgements in argcomplete.md.
#
# The scope rules A, B1-B5 and C are in macro-benchmark/README.md;
# argcomplete.md shows how this ledger applies them. In short:
# - The parser that a client passes is an argparse.ArgumentParser (annotation,
#   finders.py:40, :56, :81; B4): a method call on it is an edge to the
#   argparse method. Its actions are argparse objects that the client's
#   add_argument calls made: a package check can fix their class
#   (issubclass at finders.py:282, the safe_actions set at :286). The
#   package-created default help action and the public script parser actions
#   also retain concrete classes; arbitrary client-created actions stay opaque.
# - _patch_argument_parser (finders.py:245) gives each parser that it patches
#   a class with the bases (IntrospectiveArgumentParser, the old class), and
#   each action of it the class IntrospectAction (a subclass of the old class
#   of the action). argparse's parse_known_args then calls back
#   IntrospectiveArgumentParser._parse_known_args, which calls each action.
# - Completer roles are separate (B2). default_completer is annotated
#   BaseCompleter and admits its constructible public package subclasses
#   and BaseCompleter itself. action.completer has the ChoicesCompleter/
#   EnvironCompleter documented assignments and the SuppressCompleter test
#   assignment. The package also constructs ChoicesCompleter from choices.
#   A client function is a client callback.
# - packages._shlex.shlex is private (rule C). The package makes one shlex,
#   the lexer of split_line (lexers.py:12-14), with posix=True,
#   whitespace_split=True, debug=0, source=None, no punctuation_chars, and the
#   lexer never leaves split_line. Sites that need another state never run
#   (B1 with B2: stored values; lead's rulings on judgements 1 and 2): in
#   __init__, get_token and read_token, and also in the methods that the
#   package never calls (push_token, push_source, pop_source, sourcehook),
#   whose receiver is the same lexer (debug 0, infile None, instream a StringIO).
# - An inherited method of an outside object is named by the class of the
#   receiver (README; lead's ruling N1 at finders.py:290).
# - The tests replace os.environ with a dict and pass sys.exit as exit_method:
#   those trace edges are in argcomplete.rejected.json.
default reject argcomplete.packages._shlex.shlex.__iter__, argcomplete.packages._shlex.shlex.__next__: no shlex object is iterated, unpacked or searched with `in` at this site; the package makes one shlex, the lexer of split_line (lexers.py:12), and reads it only with get_token (lexers.py:39); the iterated and searched values are strs, lists, tuples, dicts, sets, dict views, deques, generators, os.environ, argparse objects and the lines of files

